predeterminado de la puerta de enlace para esta ejecuci√≥n.\",\n246\t      mainTimelineMessage: \"Mensaje de la l√≠nea de tiempo principal\",\n247\t      assistantTaskPrompt: \"Indicaci√≥n para la tarea del asistente\",\n248\t      deliverySection: \"Entrega\",\n249\t      deliverySub: \"Elige d√≥nde se env√≠an los res√∫menes de ejecuci√≥n.\",\n250\t      resultDelivery: \"Entrega de resultados\",\n251\t      announceDefault: \"Anunciar resumen (predeterminado)\",\n252\t      webhookPost: \"Webhook POST\",\n253\t      noneInternal: \"Ninguna (interno)\",\n254\t      deliveryHelp:\n255\t        \"Anunciar publica un resumen en el chat. Ninguna mantiene la ejecuci√≥n interna.\",\n256\t      webhookUrl: \"URL del webhook\",\n257\t      channel: \"Canal\",\n258\t      webhookPlaceholder: \"https://example.com/cron\",\n259\t      channelHelp: \"Elige qu√© canal conectado recibe el resumen.\",\n260\t      webhookHelp: \"Env√≠a res√∫menes de ejecuci√≥n a un endpoint webhook.\",\n261\t      to: \"Para\",\n262\t      toPlaceholder: \"+1555... o ID de chat\",\n263\t      toHelp: \"Anulaci√≥n opcional del destinatario (ID de chat, tel√©fono o ID de usuario).\",\n264\t      advanced: \"Avanzado\",\n265\t      advancedHelp:\n266\t        \"Anulaciones opcionales para garant√≠as de entrega, variaci√≥n de programaci√≥n y controles del modelo.\",\n267\t      deleteAfterRun: \"Eliminar despu√©s de ejecutar\",\n268\t      deleteAfterRunHelp:\n269\t        \"Ideal para recordatorios de un solo uso que deben limpiarse autom√°ticamente.\",\n270\t      clearAgentOverride: \"Limpiar anulaci√≥n de agente\",\n271\t      clearAgentHelp:\n272\t        \"Forza a esta tarea a usar el asistente predeterminado de la puerta de enlace.\",\n273\t      exactTiming: \"Tiempo exacto (sin escalonamiento)\",\n274\t      exactTimingHelp: \"Ejecutar en l√≠mites exactos de cron sin dispersi√≥n.\",\n275\t      staggerWindow: \"Ventana de escalonamiento\",\n276\t      staggerUnit: \"Unidad de escalonamiento\",\n277\t      staggerPlaceholder: \"30\",\n278\t      seconds: \"Segundos\",\n279\t      model: \"Modelo\",\n280\t      modelPlaceholder: \"openai/gpt-5.2\",\n281\t      modelHelp:\n282\t        \"Comienza a escribir para seleccionar un modelo conocido o ingresa uno personalizado.\",\n283\t      thinking: \"Pensamiento\",\n284\t      thinkingPlaceholder: \"bajo\",\n285\t      thinkingHelp: \"Usa un nivel sugerido o ingresa un valor espec√≠fico del proveedor.\",\n286\t      bestEffortDelivery: \"Entrega de mejor esfuerzo\",\n287\t      bestEffortHelp: \"No fallar la tarea si la entrega misma falla.\",\n288\t      cantAddYet: \"A√∫n no se puede agregar la tarea\",\n289\t      fillRequired: \"Completa los campos requeridos a continuaci√≥n para habilitar el env√≠o.\",\n290\t      fixFields: \"Corrige {count} campo para continuar.\",\n291\t      fixFieldsPlural: \"Corrige {count} campos para continuar.\",\n292\t      saving: \"Guardando...\",\n293\t      saveChanges: \"Guardar cambios\",\n294\t      addJob: \"Agregar tarea\",\n295\t      cancel: \"Cancelar\",\n296\t    },\n297\t    jobList: {\n298\t      allJobs: \"todas las tareas\",\n299\t      selectJob: \"(selecciona una tarea)\",\n300\t      enabled: \"habilitada\",\n301\t      disabled: \"deshabilitada\",\n302\t      edit: \"Editar\",\n303\t      clone: \"Clonar\",\n304\t      disable: \"Deshabilitar\",\n305\t      enable: \"Habilitar\",\n306\t      run: \"Ejecutar\",\n307\t      history: \"Historial\",\n308\t      remove: \"Eliminar\",\n309\t    },\n310\t    jobDetail: {\n311\t      system: \"Sistema\",\n312\t      prompt: \"Indicaci√≥n\",\n313\t      delivery: \"Entrega\",\n314\t      agent: \"Agente\",\n315\t    },\n316\t    jobState: {\n317\t      status: \"Estado\",\n318\t      next: \"Pr√≥xima\",\n319\t      last: \"√öltima\",\n320\t    },\n321\t    runEntry: {\n322\t      noSummary: \"Sin resumen.\",\n323\t      runAt: \"Ejecutada a las\",\n324\t      openRunChat: \"Abrir chat de ejecuci√≥n\",\n325\t      next: \"Pr√≥xima {rel}\",\n326\t      due: \"Programada {rel}\",\n327\t    },\n328\t    errors: {\n329\t      nameRequired: \"El nombre es requerido.\",\n330\t      scheduleAtInvalid: \"Ingresa una fecha/hora v√°lida.\",\n331\t      everyAmountInvalid: \"El intervalo debe ser mayor a 0.\",\n332\t      cronExprRequired: \"La expresi√≥n Cron es requerida.\",\n333\t      staggerAmountInvalid: \"El escalonamiento debe ser mayor a 0.\",\n334\t      systemTextRequired: \"El texto del sistema es requerido.\",\n335\t      agentMessageRequired: \"El mensaje del agente es requerido.\",\n336\t      timeoutInvalid: \"Si se establece, el tiempo de espera debe ser mayor a 0 segundos.\",\n337\t      webhookUrlRequired: \"La URL del webhook es requerida.\",\n338\t      webhookUrlInvalid: \"La URL del webhook debe comenzar con http:// o https://.\",\n339\t      invalidRunTime: \"Tiempo de ejecuci√≥n inv√°lido.\",\n340\t      invalidIntervalAmount: \"Cantidad de intervalo inv√°lida.\",\n341\t      cronExprRequiredShort: \"Expresi√≥n Cron requerida.\",\n342\t      invalidStaggerAmount: \"Cantidad de escalonamiento inv√°lida.\",\n343\t      systemEventTextRequired: \"Texto de evento del sistema requerido.\",\n344\t      agentMessageRequiredShort: \"Mensaje del agente requerido.\",\n345\t      nameRequiredShort: \"Nombre requerido.\",\n346\t    },\n347\t  },\n348\t};\n349\t"},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ATU5NbCxTH25GeEtMCB6XY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\timport { afterEach, beforeEach, describe, expect, it, vi } from \"vitest\";\n2\timport { pt_BR } from \"../locales/pt-BR.ts\";\n3\timport { zh_CN } from \"../locales/zh-CN.ts\";\n4\timport { zh_TW } from \"../locales/zh-TW.ts\";\n5\t\n6\ttype TranslateModule = typeof import(\"../lib/translate.ts\");\n7\t\n8\tfunction createStorageMock(): Storage {\n9\t  const store = new Map<string, string>();\n10\t  return {\n11\t    get length() {\n12\t      return store.size;\n13\t    },\n14\t    clear() {\n15\t      store.clear();\n16\t    },\n17\t    getItem(key: string) {\n18\t      return store.get(key) ?? null;\n19\t    },\n20\t    key(index: number) {\n21\t      return Array.from(store.keys())[index] ?? null;\n22\t    },\n23\t    removeItem(key: string) {\n24\t      store.delete(key);\n25\t    },\n26\t    setItem(key: string, value: string) {\n27\t      store.set(key, String(value));\n28\t    },\n29\t  };\n30\t}\n31\t\n32\tdescribe(\"i18n\", () => {\n33\t  let translate: TranslateModule;\n34\t\n35\t  beforeEach(async () => {\n36\t    vi.resetModules();\n37\t    vi.stubGlobal(\"localStorage\", createStorageMock());\n38\t    vi.stubGlobal(\"navigator\", { language: \"en-US\" } as Navigator);\n39\t    translate = await import(\"../lib/translate.ts\");\n40\t    localStorage.clear();\n41\t    // Reset to English\n42\t    await translate.i18n.setLocale(\"en\");\n43\t  });\n44\t\n45\t  afterEach(() => {\n46\t    vi.unstubAllGlobals();\n47\t  });\n48\t\n49\t  it(\"should return the key if translation is missing\", () => {\n50\t    expect(translate.t(\"non.existent.key\")).toBe(\"non.existent.key\");\n51\t  });\n52\t\n53\t  it(\"should return the correct English translation\", () => {\n54\t    expect(translate.t(\"common.health\")).toBe(\"Health\");\n55\t  });\n56\t\n57\t  it(\"should replace parameters correctly\", () => {\n58\t    expect(translate.t(\"overview.stats.cronNext\", { time: \"10:00\" })).toBe(\"Next wake 10:00\");\n59\t  });\n60\t\n61\t  it(\"should fallback to English if key is missing in another locale\", async () => {\n62\t    // We haven't registered other locales in the test environment yet,\n63\t    // but the logic should fallback to 'en' map which is always there.\n64\t    await translate.i18n.setLocale(\"zh-CN\");\n65\t    // Since we don't mock the import, it might fail to load zh-CN,\n66\t    // but let's assume it falls back to English for now.\n67\t    expect(translate.t(\"common.health\")).toBeDefined();\n68\t  });\n69\t\n70\t  it(\"loads translations even when setting the same locale again\", async () => {\n71\t    const internal = translate.i18n as unknown as {\n72\t      locale: string;\n73\t      translations: Record<string, unknown>;\n74\t    };\n75\t    internal.locale = \"zh-CN\";\n76\t    delete internal.translations[\"zh-CN\"];\n77\t\n78\t    await translate.i18n.setLocale(\"zh-CN\");\n79\t    expect(translate.t(\"common.health\")).toBe(\"ÂÅ•Â∫∑Áä∂ÂÜµ\");\n80\t  });\n81\t\n82\t  it(\"loads saved non-English locale on startup\", async () => {\n83\t    vi.resetModules();\n84\t    vi.stubGlobal(\"localStorage\", createStorageMock());\n85\t    vi.stubGlobal(\"navigator\", { language: \"en-US\" } as Navigator);\n86\t    localStorage.setItem(\"openclaw.i18n.locale\", \"zh-CN\");\n87\t    const fresh = await import(\"../lib/translate.ts\");\n88\t    await vi.waitFor(() => {\n89\t      expect(fresh.i18n.getLocale()).toBe(\"zh-CN\");\n90\t    });\n91\t    expect(fresh.i18n.getLocale()).toBe(\"zh-CN\");\n92\t    expect(fresh.t(\"common.health\")).toBe(\"ÂÅ•Â∫∑Áä∂ÂÜµ\");\n93\t  });\n94\t\n95\t  it(\"skips node localStorage accessors that warn without a storage file\", async () => {\n96\t    vi.resetModules();\n97\t    vi.unstubAllGlobals();\n98\t    vi.stubGlobal(\"navigator\", { language: \"en-US\" } as Navigator);\n99\t    const warningSpy = vi.spyOn(process, \"emitWarning\");\n100\t\n101\t    const fresh = await import(\"../lib/translate.ts\");\n102\t\n103\t    expect(fresh.i18n.getLocale()).toBe(\"en\");\n104\t    expect(warningSpy).not.toHaveBeenCalledWith(\n105\t      \"`--localstorage-file` was provided without a valid path\",\n106\t      expect.anything(),\n107\t      expect.anything(),\n108\t    );\n109\t  });\n110\t\n111\t  it(\"keeps the version label available in shipped locales\", () => {\n112\t    expect((pt_BR.common as { version?: string }).version).toBeTruthy();\n113\t    expect((zh_CN.common as { version?: string }).version).toBeTruthy();\n114\t    expect((zh_TW.common as { version?: string }).version).toBeTruthy();\n115\t  });\n116\t});\n117\t"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I have everything I need. Let me write the plan."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H3sNJSEmCsyXjXCkC2t2uA","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/root/.claude/plans/sharded-weaving-axolotl.md","content":"# Plan: Add French (fr) Language Support\n\n## Context\n\nIssue #3460 requests French language support in the OpenClaw UI. The UI uses a custom TypeScript i18n system (no external library) with lazy-loaded locale files under `ui/src/i18n/locales/`. Currently 6 languages are supported: `en`, `zh-CN`, `zh-TW`, `pt-BR`, `de`, `es`. Adding French requires changes to 4 files and creation of 1 new file.\n\n## Files to Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `ui/src/i18n/lib/types.ts` | Add `\"fr\"` to the `Locale` union type |\n| `ui/src/i18n/lib/registry.ts` | Register `fr` in `LAZY_LOCALES`, `LAZY_LOCALE_REGISTRY`, and `resolveNavigatorLocale` |\n| `ui/src/i18n/locales/en.ts` | Add `fr` key to the `languages` section |\n| `ui/src/i18n/locales/fr.ts` | **New file** ‚Äî complete French translation map |\n\n## Step-by-Step Changes\n\n### 1. `ui/src/i18n/lib/types.ts`\nAdd `\"fr\"` to the `Locale` union:\n```ts\nexport type Locale = \"en\" | \"zh-CN\" | \"zh-TW\" | \"pt-BR\" | \"de\" | \"es\" | \"fr\";\n```\n\n### 2. `ui/src/i18n/lib/registry.ts`\n- Add `\"fr\"` to `LAZY_LOCALES` array\n- Add `fr` entry to `LAZY_LOCALE_REGISTRY` with `exportName: \"fr\"` and `loader: () => import(\"../locales/fr.ts\")`\n- Add `if (navLang.startsWith(\"fr\")) return \"fr\";` to `resolveNavigatorLocale`\n\n### 3. `ui/src/i18n/locales/en.ts` ‚Äî `languages` section\nAdd one line:\n```ts\nfr: \"Fran√ßais (French)\",\n```\n\n### 4. New file: `ui/src/i18n/locales/fr.ts`\nFull French translation following the exact structure of `es.ts` / `en.ts`. All top-level keys: `common`, `nav`, `tabs`, `subtitles`, `overview`, `login`, `chat`, `languages`, `cron` (with all sub-keys). Must include `common.version` so the existing test at `translate.test.ts:111-115` continues to pass if extended.\n\nKey translation decisions:\n- `common.version` ‚Üí `\"Version\"` (same, used as label)\n- `nav.agent` ‚Üí `\"Agent\"`, `nav.settings` ‚Üí `\"Param√®tres\"`\n- `tabs.cron` ‚Üí `\"T√¢ches Cron\"`, `tabs.skills` ‚Üí `\"Comp√©tences\"`\n- `overview.access.title` ‚Üí `\"Acc√®s √† la passerelle\"`\n- `languages.fr` ‚Üí `\"Fran√ßais\"` (self-referential, no parenthetical needed)\n- All other language names in French: `languages.en` ‚Üí `\"Anglais (English)\"`, etc.\n\n## Existing Patterns to Follow\n\n- `es.ts` is the most complete non-English locale ‚Äî use it as the structural template\n- Export name must match the locale key exactly: `export const fr: TranslationMap = { ... }`\n- Only include keys that differ meaningfully from English (the system falls back to `en` for missing keys), but for completeness follow what `es.ts` does (full coverage)\n- Technical terms like `Tailscale`, `WebSocket`, `Cron`, `IANA`, `HTTPS` stay untranslated\n\n## No Test Changes Required\n\nThe existing test at line 111-115 only checks `pt_BR`, `zh_CN`, `zh_TW` ‚Äî it will continue to pass. No new test cases are needed for `fr` since the pattern is already covered.\n\n## Verification\n\nAfter implementation:\n```bash\npnpm build        # Check for TypeScript errors and [INEFFECTIVE_DYNAMIC_IMPORT] warnings\npnpm test -- ui/src/i18n/test/translate.test.ts   # Run i18n tests\npnpm check        # Lint + format check\n```\n\nManually: set `localStorage.setItem(\"openclaw.i18n.locale\", \"fr\")` in the browser and reload the UI to confirm French strings render.\n"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H3sNJSEmCsyXjXCkC2t2uA","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /root/.claude/plans/sharded-weaving-axolotl.md\n\n<system-reminder>\nThe task tools haven't been used recently. If you're working on tasks that would benefit from tracking progress, consider using TaskCreate to add new tasks and TaskUpdate to update task status (set to in_progress when starting, completed when done). Also consider cleaning up the task list if it has become stale. Only use these if relevant to the current work. This is just a gentle reminder - ignore if not applicable. Make sure that you NEVER mention this reminder to the user\n\n</system-reminder>"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SHjDB7C4Uaw8AxgvM4u5qM","name":"ExitPlanMode","input":{}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"User has approved your plan. You can now start coding. Start with updating your todo list if applicable\n\nYour plan has been saved to: /root/.claude/plans/sharded-weaving-axolotl.md\nYou can refer back to it if needed during implementation.\n\n## Approved Plan:\n# Plan: Add French (fr) Language Support\n\n## Context\n\nIssue #3460 requests French language support in the OpenClaw UI. The UI uses a custom TypeScript i18n system (no external library) with lazy-loaded locale files under `ui/src/i18n/locales/`. Currently 6 languages are supported: `en`, `zh-CN`, `zh-TW`, `pt-BR`, `de`, `es`. Adding French requires changes to 4 files and creation of 1 new file.\n\n## Files to Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `ui/src/i18n/lib/types.ts` | Add `\"fr\"` to the `Locale` union type |\n| `ui/src/i18n/lib/registry.ts` | Register `fr` in `LAZY_LOCALES`, `LAZY_LOCALE_REGISTRY`, and `resolveNavigatorLocale` |\n| `ui/src/i18n/locales/en.ts` | Add `fr` key to the `languages` section |\n| `ui/src/i18n/locales/fr.ts` | **New file** ‚Äî complete French translation map |\n\n## Step-by-Step Changes\n\n### 1. `ui/src/i18n/lib/types.ts`\nAdd `\"fr\"` to the `Locale` union:\n```ts\nexport type Locale = \"en\" | \"zh-CN\" | \"zh-TW\" | \"pt-BR\" | \"de\" | \"es\" | \"fr\";\n```\n\n### 2. `ui/src/i18n/lib/registry.ts`\n- Add `\"fr\"` to `LAZY_LOCALES` array\n- Add `fr` entry to `LAZY_LOCALE_REGISTRY` with `exportName: \"fr\"` and `loader: () => import(\"../locales/fr.ts\")`\n- Add `if (navLang.startsWith(\"fr\")) return \"fr\";` to `resolveNavigatorLocale`\n\n### 3. `ui/src/i18n/locales/en.ts` ‚Äî `languages` section\nAdd one line:\n```ts\nfr: \"Fran√ßais (French)\",\n```\n\n### 4. New file: `ui/src/i18n/locales/fr.ts`\nFull French translation following the exact structure of `es.ts` / `en.ts`. All top-level keys: `common`, `nav`, `tabs`, `subtitles`, `overview`, `login`, `chat`, `languages`, `cron` (with all sub-keys). Must include `common.version` so the existing test at `translate.test.ts:111-115` continues to pass if extended.\n\nKey translation decisions:\n- `common.version` ‚Üí `\"Version\"` (same, used as label)\n- `nav.agent` ‚Üí `\"Agent\"`, `nav.settings` ‚Üí `\"Param√®tres\"`\n- `tabs.cron` ‚Üí `\"T√¢ches Cron\"`, `tabs.skills` ‚Üí `\"Comp√©tences\"`\n- `overview.access.title` ‚Üí `\"Acc√®s √† la passerelle\"`\n- `languages.fr` ‚Üí `\"Fran√ßais\"` (self-referential, no parenthetical needed)\n- All other language names in French: `languages.en` ‚Üí `\"Anglais (English)\"`, etc.\n\n## Existing Patterns to Follow\n\n- `es.ts` is the most complete non-English locale ‚Äî use it as the structural template\n- Export name must match the locale key exactly: `export const fr: TranslationMap = { ... }`\n- Only include keys that differ meaningfully from English (the system falls back to `en` for missing keys), but for completeness follow what `es.ts` does (full coverage)\n- Technical terms like `Tailscale`, `WebSocket`, `Cron`, `IANA`, `HTTPS` stay untranslated\n\n## No Test Changes Required\n\nThe existing test at line 111-115 only checks `pt_BR`, `zh_CN`, `zh_TW` ‚Äî it will continue to pass. No new test cases are needed for `fr` since the pattern is already covered.\n\n## Verification\n\nAfter implementation:\n```bash\npnpm build        # Check for TypeScript errors and [INEFFECTIVE_DYNAMIC_IMPORT] warnings\npnpm test -- ui/src/i18n/test/translate.test.ts   # Run i18n tests\npnpm check        # Lint + format check\n```\n\nManually: set `localStorage.setItem(\"openclaw.i18n.locale\", \"fr\")` in the browser and reload the UI to confirm French strings render.\n\n<system-reminder>\n## Exited Plan Mode\n\nYou have exited plan mode. You can now make edits, run tools, and take actions. The plan file is located at /root/.claude/plans/sharded-weaving-axolotl.md if you need to reference it.\n</system-reminder>","tool_use_id":"toolu_01SHjDB7C4Uaw8AxgvM4u5qM"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TdD4VPKG8w7BUQGUrRN6D2","name":"TaskCreate","input":{"subject":"Add French (fr) i18n support","description":"Create fr.ts locale file and update types.ts, registry.ts, en.ts to register French as a supported language."}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TdD4VPKG8w7BUQGUrRN6D2","type":"tool_result","content":"Task #1 created successfully: Add French (fr) i18n support"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XAptgvLyDJzG3mGzNqt4K8","name":"TaskUpdate","input":{"taskId":"1","status":"in_progress"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XAptgvLyDJzG3mGzNqt4K8","type":"tool_result","content":"Updated task #1 status"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"First, create the branch and make all edits in parallel:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011J8dy3DBMRjsJcp7jBvhjV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git checkout -b feat/french-i18n","description":"Create feature branch for French i18n"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011J8dy3DBMRjsJcp7jBvhjV","type":"tool_result","content":"Switched to a new branch 'feat/french-i18n'","is_error":false}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WnTSmjcnSbpqYTGaiquNVM","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/workspace/ui/src/i18n/lib/types.ts","old_string":"export type Locale = \"en\" | \"zh-CN\" | \"zh-TW\" | \"pt-BR\" | \"de\" | \"es\";","new_string":"export type Locale = \"en\" | \"zh-CN\" | \"zh-TW\" | \"pt-BR\" | \"de\" | \"es\" | \"fr\";"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WnTSmjcnSbpqYTGaiquNVM","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/ui/src/i18n/lib/types.ts has been updated successfully."}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GW37cQW2WdtZTaEqJKrngu","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/workspace/ui/src/i18n/lib/registry.ts","old_string":"const LAZY_LOCALES: readonly LazyLocale[] = [\"zh-CN\", \"zh-TW\", \"pt-BR\", \"de\", \"es\"];","new_string":"const LAZY_LOCALES: readonly LazyLocale[] = [\"zh-CN\", \"zh-TW\", \"pt-BR\", \"de\", \"es\", \"fr\"];"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GW37cQW2WdtZTaEqJKrngu","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/ui/src/i18n/lib/registry.ts has been updated successfully."}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HRzF9P1w4nPWVSoQep8i5C","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/workspace/ui/src/i18n/lib/registry.ts","old_string":"  es: {\n    exportName: \"es\",\n    loader: () => import(\"../locales/es.ts\"),\n  },\n};","new_string":"  es: {\n    exportName: \"es\",\n    loader: () => import(\"../locales/es.ts\"),\n  },\n  fr: {\n    exportName: \"fr\",\n    loader: () => import(\"../locales/fr.ts\"),\n  },\n};"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HRzF9P1w4nPWVSoQep8i5C","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/ui/src/i18n/lib/registry.ts has been updated successfully."}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017nnz65qMMqfmmWese5CxfM","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/workspace/ui/src/i18n/lib/registry.ts","old_string":"  if (navLang.startsWith(\"es\")) {\n    return \"es\";\n  }\n  return DEFAULT_LOCALE;","new_string":"  if (navLang.startsWith(\"es\")) {\n    return \"es\";\n  }\n  if (navLang.star